        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When a tankless water heater stops heating, read the code, then check in order: power and settings, flow at the fixture, gas supply, scale, and the vent and condensate drain. Run the crossover test if the water is lukewarm everywhere, and check every breaker on an electric unit. Most causes are found without opening the cabinet.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Leave gas pressure, burners, boards and wiring to a licensed technician, and call one immediately for any vent damage or CO alarm. If scale was the cause, test your water hardness and descale on a schedule, because the next failure from scale is the one that ends the heat exchanger.
          </p>
        </div>

